$$
3 \text{ sprints} \times 3 \text{ days} = 9 \text{ sprints}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate the Total Distance Ran
Each sprint is **60 meters**, so the total distance covered in a week is:

$$
9 \text{ sprints} \times 60 \text{ meters/sprint} = 540 \text{ meters}
$$

---

### Final Answer:
$$
\boxed{540}
$$

