To determine how many **dozens of eggs** Claire will consume in **4 weeks**, we can break the problem into logical steps based on the information provided:

---

### Step 1: Eggs per Day
Claire makes a **3-egg omelet every morning**.  
So, she consumes **3 eggs per day**.

---

### Step 2: Days in 4 Weeks
A week has **7 days**, so in **4 weeks**, the number of days is:
$$
4 \text{ weeks} \times 7 \text{ days/week} = 28 \text{ days}
$$

---

### Step 3: Total Eggs Consumed in 4 Weeks
Multiplying the daily egg consumption by the number of days:
$$
3 \text{ eggs/day} \times 28 \text{ days} = 84 \text{ eggs}
$$

---

### Step 4: Convert Eggs to Dozens
Since one **dozen = 12 eggs**, to find out how many **dozens** of eggs 84 eggs represent:
$$
\frac{84 \text{ eggs}}{12 \text{ eggs/dozen}} = 7 \text{ dozen}
$$

---

### Final Answer:
$$
\boxed{7}
$$

Claire will eat **7 dozen eggs** in 4 weeks. 🥚🍳🧮

